From 0c26a07458ce9afcd134041659a5ca3cf273f880 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:45:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DVBridge: content mapping v4.0, a second automatic choice for
 a video without trims

The setting of the content mapping v4.0 gains "Automatic 2: no trims in
the video": dovi_tool's default v4.0 part is added to a stream whose
first RPU has neither a v4.0 part nor a level 2 block, decided once a
stream, whatever the peaks. Level 2 is what ETSI GS CCM 001 V1.1.1
calls the "Trim Pass": the colourist's trims for target displays. The
default v4.0 part carries no trims of its own (no level 8), so where a
stream has no level 2 either, adding it sets no trim of the colourist
aside, and a TV of display management 4 maps the picture with its own
newer mapping from level 1 alone. That is the one condition here that
the metadata themselves justify; "Automatic" (mastered brighter than
the display) stays as the other choice.

With either automatic choice, a later frame that brings what the choice
was made without (a v4.0 part of its own; with Automatic 2, also a
level 2 block) turns the addition off for the rest of the stream, once:
the video goes on as it is, and the display changes its mapping once
instead of back and forth. kodi.log says it.

avdvplus's rules were read as data (its strings and release notes, no
code of it run): its "CMv2.9 without L2 trims" mode and both of its
automatic modes append where an RPU carries no L2 trim, which is the
condition taken here. Its "Auto" also appends where the display's peak
is at or above the source's mastering peak, and its "Auto 2" decides
per frame from the level 1 peak against the display's peak plus a
headroom. Neither is taken: no public source says what display
management 4 does better where no compression is needed, and a choice
made per frame changes the version of the metadata within a film, which
makes a TV change its mapping (SamuriHL's note that the TV resyncs when
the version changes).

The default stays "As in the video". The player information gives
"v2.9 + v4.0 added (automatic 2: no trims in the video)". English and
Spanish.
